#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068354 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "369ac89b-e838-5929-ba71-d74b3b06445b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-10013" :question/problem "Solve the equation $x^2 -10x = -24$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $x^2 -10x +25$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\nx^2 -10x +25 = (x-5)^2\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 10x &= -24 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot x &= -24 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot x + 5^{2} - 5^{2} &= -24 \\\\\n(x - 5)^{2} - 25 &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $25$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} - 25 + 25 &= -24 + 25 \\\\\n(x - 5)^{2} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} &= 1 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x - 5)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{1} \\\\\n\\mid x - 5 \\mid &= 1 \\\\\nx - 5 &= ± 1 \\\\\nx &= 5 ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= 5 - 1 = 4 \\\\\nx_{2} &= 5 + 1 = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/id #uuid "a0cb3fb6-5ff3-5f4e-9bb9-35c88a22fd34" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-1431" :question/problem "Write the equation $x^2 + 6x +5= 0$ in the form $(x+p)^2=q$, and hence solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 6x + 5 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} + 6x &= -5 \\\\\nx^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x &= -5 \\\\\nx^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x + 3^{2} - 3^{2} &= -5 \\\\\n(x^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x + 3^{2}) - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} - 9 &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 3)^{2} - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} &= -5 + 9 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=3$ and $q=4$. Now, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 3)^{2} &= 4 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x + 3)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n\\mid x + 3 \\mid &= 2 \\\\\nx + 3 &= ± 2 \\\\\nx &= -3 ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= -3 + 2 =-1 \\\\\nx_{2} &= -3 - 2 =-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/id #uuid "d53f36b5-fc95-55de-b716-789dd327d2f8" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-1432" :question/problem "Solve the equation $x^2-2x-1=0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 2x - 1 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2x &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot x &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot x + 1^{2} - 1^{2} &= 1 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2x + 1) - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} &= 2 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x - 1)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n\\mid x - 1 \\mid &= \\sqrt{2} \\\\\nx - 1 &= ± \\sqrt{2} \\\\\nx &= 1 ± \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our solutions are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= 1 + \\sqrt{2}, \\\\\nx_{2} &= 1 - \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82128d4e-90ce-54e6-9139-be770a78c0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065693} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c547ca-8084-5908-97de-3f03cc639af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065694} {:answer/id #uuid "e65bf10a-6021-5c9a-b346-04af974d42eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065695} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c4f340-cdf8-5830-8db3-822e954bb964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065696} {:answer/id #uuid "07a9f04a-35e6-50da-82a2-66f5b5f3c581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82128d4e-90ce-54e6-9139-be770a78c0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065693} :answer-field/id #uuid "28535634-27c2-5f2d-8219-b57b1c62ccb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065692}] :question/id #uuid "22f36eaf-d2b6-5e47-8cc3-19f122968355" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-141624" :question/problem "Let $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation $x^{2} - 2x = 24$. Find the value $x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2}$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $x^{2} - 2x + 1$ is a perfect square.*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824db7a0-468b-5b7c-bdd3-7bd19185dd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066672} {:answer/id #uuid "f44af2a5-1591-5f5e-93ba-40c0ddd584b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-8 ± 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066673} {:answer/id #uuid "30dfca08-4199-59da-8d02-2600e0f2122b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 75, z = 5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066674} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3b9749-a33c-5c57-89ac-26939f855dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z = 5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066675} {:answer/id #uuid "6d135e5e-ebb4-5c27-84bf-0be68ee6c029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q =-70, z = ± \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824db7a0-468b-5b7c-bdd3-7bd19185dd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066672} :answer-field/id #uuid "988361f0-82f8-5fa0-bce8-8775fead2e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066671}] :question/id #uuid "5c0076f5-08a5-5d4c-9789-196650ab8295" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-3435" :question/problem "The equation $z^{2} - 50 =-10z$ can be written in the form $(z + p)^{2} = q$. Find $p + q$, and solve the equation."}]}
